    [38;5;153mStringIO[39m ([38;5;153mlineterminator="\n"[39m) so account IDs containing commas or quotes are escaped correctly rather than
    hand-joined.
  - [38;5;153mrender_json(day, rows) -> str[39m — [38;5;153m{"day": "2026-09-11", "rows": [{"account_id": "acct-1", "cents": 1050}], [39m
    [38;5;153m"total_cents": 13325}[39m, via [38;5;153mjson.dumps(..., indent=2)[39m with a trailing newline. It takes [38;5;153mday[39m where the other two
    don't; that asymmetry is deliberate, since the day is part of the document's identity once the file leaves the
    machine.

  Both are pure functions over the same [38;5;153mSequence[tuple[str, int]][39m [38;5;153mdaily_rows[39m already returns, so they stay testable
  without a database, matching the existing test.

  [1mNew [38;5;153mexport[39m command in [38;5;153mcli.py[0m, a sibling of [38;5;153msummarize[39m:

  reportkit export --day 2026-09-11 --format csv --out /var/reports/billing-2026-09-11.csv [--force]

  [38;5;153m--day[39m, [38;5;153m--format[39m ([38;5;153mclick.Choice(["csv", "json"])[39m), and [38;5;153m--out[39m are all required; no default directory, no derived names.
  [38;5;153m--format[39m excludes [38;5;153mtext[39m — the emailed summary is what [38;5;153msummarize[39m is for — and adding it later is one entry in the [38;5;153mChoice
[39m  list plus a branch.

  [1mFile handling:[0m open with mode [38;5;153m"x"[39m normally and [38;5;153m"w"[39m under [38;5;153m--force[39m, rather than checking [38;5;153mout.exists()[39m first. Same
  behavior you asked for, minus the window where something else creates the file between the check and the write. A
  [38;5;153mFileExistsError[39m becomes [38;5;153mclick.ClickException(f"{out} already exists; pass --force to overwrite.")[39m — stderr, exit 1. A
  missing parent directory also fails rather than being created; [38;5;153mexport[39m writes files, it doesn't provision paths.

  [1mTesting.[0m [38;5;153mrender_csv[39m and [38;5;153mrender_json[39m get direct cases in [38;5;153mtests/test_summarize.py[39m, following the existing pure-function
  pattern — including an account ID with a comma, to pin the quoting. A new [38;5;153mtests/test_cli.py[39m uses click's [38;5;153mCliRunner[39m in
  an isolated filesystem for three behaviors: writes the file, refuses an existing path with exit 1, and replaces it
  under [38;5;153m--force[39m. Those tests monkeypatch [38;5;153mconnect[39m and [38;5;153mdaily_rows[39m as imported into [38;5;153mreportkit.cli[39m, since the repo has no
  database fixtures and I'm not adding a Postgres dependency to the suite for a file-writing test.

